License texts of the code inside the pinned sherpa-onnx archive
(packaging/sherpa-onnx.env: sherpa-onnx-v1.13.8-linux-x64-static-no-tts-lib).

The archive holds only static libraries, no license files, so these texts were
fetched once from each component's upstream repository, at the version that
sherpa-onnx v1.13.8 pins in its cmake/*.cmake files (kissfft and kaldifst are
pinned one level down, by kaldi-native-fbank and kaldi-decoder), and are kept
unchanged.
scripts/gen-copyright takes license texts from here for debian/copyright, and
the koeinput package installs onnxruntime-1.28.2-ThirdPartyNotices.txt.

When the pin changes, fetch the files again at the new versions, update this
list and run scripts/gen-copyright.

